        "text_rBz8q3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Planning a deck in New York usually begins with a few big questions: Should you hire a deck builder, purchase the materials yourself or use a professionally engineered system that arrives prepared for assembly?<br/><br/>This guide explains the main options, what affects the cost, how permits work, what to ask a contractor and how to choose between pressure-treated wood and composite decking.<br/><br/>A-DIY offers a third way to complete the project: a professionally engineered deck system delivered with coordinated components prepared for assembly. You can build it yourself or hire a local handyman, carpenter or contractor to help.<br/><br/></p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        },
        "button_6jfzcR": {
